config IO
	bool "io: byte stream reader and writer interfaces"
	default y
	select STATUS
	help
	  The el_reader and el_writer interfaces, helpers built on them,
	  readers and writers over caller-provided memory, and the contract
	  test suite for backends. Freestanding: needs only memcpy().

config IO_POSIX
	bool "io_posix: POSIX file descriptor backend"
	default y
	depends on IO && PLATFORM_POSIX
	help
	  Reader and writer over a file descriptor the caller owns, using
	  read(2) and write(2). Available only when the toolchain provides
	  <unistd.h>.

config IO_ALLOC
	bool "io_alloc: a writer that grows, over an allocator"
	default y
	depends on IO && ALLOC
	help
	  el_grow_writer: an el_writer that collects what is written in
	  memory from an el_allocator, growing as needed. It is the one part
	  of io that needs alloc: turn it off and io builds and links no
	  allocator. Freestanding: needs memcpy().
